  "protocolVersion": null,
  "instructions": "Bluet holds this product's decisions, rules (gotchas), intent and open questions — the things the code does not say.\n\n1. Before changing code, call bluet_preflight with the product and the task (and the files you expect to touch). Follow the rules it returns; they record what went wrong before.\n2. Before committing, call bluet_check with the plan or diff. A \"blocking\" conflict means stop and ask the user.\n3. When you finish work that settled something (a choice between options, a constraint, a trap you hit), call bluet_debrief. It proposes; the owner decides.\n\nUse bluet_products_list if you do not know the product slug. Never record a decision the user did not make — propose it.",
